1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,345
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,471 --> 00:00:54,305
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,264
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,431 --> 00:00:56,265
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:08,944
TIN CAN BASTARD

6
00:01:09,111 --> 00:01:11,113
The offer for your return to directing
still stands.

7
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:12,531
I'll wait for your call.

8
00:01:13,449 --> 00:01:15,034
Just give me a week.

9
00:01:15,159 --> 00:01:17,703
I can secure
all of last year's quarterly data.

10
00:01:26,212 --> 00:01:27,087
Deok-sun?

11
00:01:27,213 --> 00:01:28,047
Yes.

12
00:01:28,172 --> 00:01:30,216
The Haemado guesthouse owner's niece.

13
00:01:30,341 --> 00:01:32,760
The teen who looks like Ssuk?

14
00:01:32,885 --> 00:01:34,011
-Yes.
-Wait.

15
00:01:34,136 --> 00:01:35,304
You met again at work?

16
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:37,181
She's been working there for a while.

17
00:01:38,057 --> 00:01:39,683
She joined our team last week.

18
00:01:41,602 --> 00:01:42,770
Is she pretty?

19
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,524
What? She's younger than Wan-do.

20
00:01:50,236 --> 00:01:52,196
Even back then, she wasn't exactly normal.

21
00:01:52,321 --> 00:01:53,864
Early winter weather is setting in.

22
00:01:53,989 --> 00:01:54,990
But she grew up…

23
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:57,535
to be quite a brat.

24
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:00,746
Must've been nice to see her.
You talked about her sometimes.

25
00:02:00,871 --> 00:02:04,041
Officials say that in the early hours
of the 24th or 25th,

26
00:02:04,166 --> 00:02:07,086
rain will fall nationwide,
dropping temperatures,

27
00:02:07,211 --> 00:02:09,505
and potentially turning into snow.

28
00:02:10,256 --> 00:02:12,258
This year, Seoul's first snow is expected

29
00:02:12,383 --> 00:02:14,593
to arrive 11 days earlier than last year.

30
00:02:14,718 --> 00:02:15,886
We hope Seoul

31
00:02:16,011 --> 00:02:18,097
will see its first snow very soon.

32
00:02:18,222 --> 00:02:19,390
Where should we watch it?

33
00:02:20,891 --> 00:02:22,810
The playground?
We haven't been in a while.

34
00:02:23,602 --> 00:02:24,562
Sure, let's do it.

35
00:02:29,358 --> 00:02:35,239
4. ARE WE DREAMING THE SAME DREAM?

36
00:02:36,323 --> 00:02:38,242
No way! Is it really Park Yong-dae?
The athlete?

37
00:02:38,367 --> 00:02:40,703
He has that dragon tattoo.
It's him without a doubt.

38
00:02:40,828 --> 00:02:42,204
An article revealed his initials.

39
00:02:42,329 --> 00:02:44,582
-Did you see the article?
-Hey.

40
00:02:44,707 --> 00:02:47,626
Someone posted that online a week ago,
and it went viral.

41
00:02:47,751 --> 00:02:49,837
Park Yong-dae is known for this.

42
00:02:49,962 --> 00:02:52,131
-That's why he got divorced.
-I knew it.

43
00:02:52,256 --> 00:02:55,759
At the scene of last week's motel fire,
an ex-international turned K League coach…

44
00:02:55,885 --> 00:02:56,969
I'll be out of touch for a while.

45
00:02:57,094 --> 00:02:58,095
SU-YEON
I'LL BE OUT OF TOUCH FOR A WHILE

46
00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:00,514
…was confirmed to have been
with a same-sex partner,

47
00:03:00,639 --> 00:03:02,641
causing a stir in the sports world.

48
00:03:03,934 --> 00:03:05,644
The K League and Mr. P…

49
00:03:05,769 --> 00:03:07,313
I'm not mad. Call me.

50
00:03:07,438 --> 00:03:10,190
…have not released
an official statement yet.

51
00:03:10,316 --> 00:03:13,611
The industry is reportedly
considering legal action.

52
00:03:13,736 --> 00:03:15,070
HIDING WON'T SOLVE ANYTHING

53
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:17,489
Human rights organizations say
this case highlights

54
00:03:17,615 --> 00:03:19,241
public figures' privacy issues

55
00:03:19,366 --> 00:03:21,410
and discrimination
based on sexual orientation,

56
00:03:21,535 --> 00:03:23,162
and argued for better protection
of their human rights…

57
00:03:23,287 --> 00:03:24,121
Is that Park Yong-dae?

58
00:03:24,246 --> 00:03:25,331
FERRY TERMINAL
TICKETS

59
00:03:25,456 --> 00:03:26,749
…and respect for diversity.

60
00:03:26,874 --> 00:03:28,000
Hey!

61
00:03:28,125 --> 00:03:29,585
Wait up.

62
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:31,587
Come on, wait for me!

63
00:03:34,590 --> 00:03:36,467
Your aunt will meet you there.

64
00:03:38,636 --> 00:03:40,220
Jeez.

65
00:03:40,346 --> 00:03:41,388
Hey.

66
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:43,557
Take this.

67
00:03:44,475 --> 00:03:46,018
Your feet always get cold.

68
00:03:46,143 --> 00:03:47,478
You need your bed socks.

69
00:03:49,021 --> 00:03:50,689
Mr. Lee from Handel Piano Academy.

70
00:03:53,901 --> 00:03:56,403
The second son of Pastor Kwon
from New Hope Church.

71
00:03:56,528 --> 00:03:58,405
The husband of Lucky Hair Salon's owner.

72
00:03:58,530 --> 00:04:00,532
The police officer
who lived in Daehu Apartments.

73
00:04:00,658 --> 00:04:02,493
Did you think I didn't know?

74
00:04:02,618 --> 00:04:05,037
I've known everything since I was nine.

75
00:04:09,041 --> 00:04:10,459
Look, Su-a--

76
00:04:10,584 --> 00:04:11,585
But Dad.

77
00:04:12,169 --> 00:04:15,089
How could you do it with my friend's dad?

78
00:04:19,551 --> 00:04:20,386
I did it.

79
00:04:21,887 --> 00:04:25,140
I'm the one who posted it online.

80
00:04:26,350 --> 00:04:28,477
I hope everyone criticizes you.

81
00:04:50,457 --> 00:04:52,209
NO INTERNET SERVICE

82
00:05:00,926 --> 00:05:02,553
HAEMADO GUESTHOUSE

83
00:05:16,525 --> 00:05:23,407
HERO FROM HAEMADO
NATIONAL TEAM SOCCER PLAYER PARK YONG-DAE

84
00:05:23,532 --> 00:05:24,575
HAEMADO

85
00:05:27,661 --> 00:05:29,455
HERO FROM HAEMADO
NATIONAL TEAM SOCCER PLAYER PARK YONG-DAE

86
00:05:46,889 --> 00:05:48,098
Excuse me.

87
00:06:05,616 --> 00:06:08,160
Which way is the bus stop?

88
00:06:22,549 --> 00:06:23,759
Hang this up first.

89
00:06:23,884 --> 00:06:25,636
-All right.
-Wow, it's big.

90
00:06:25,761 --> 00:06:27,346
-Wow.
-Here, grab this.

91
00:06:27,471 --> 00:06:28,889
-Nice.
-Looks great.

92
00:06:29,014 --> 00:06:30,015
-Here.
-That'll do.

93
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:33,977
Looks like he ran away here
because he caused trouble on the mainland.

94
00:06:34,686 --> 00:06:35,562
What trouble?

95
00:06:36,313 --> 00:06:39,483
Maybe he's the one
who ruined the mural at the dock.

96
00:06:39,608 --> 00:06:42,361
He's the only outsider here.

97
00:06:42,486 --> 00:06:44,613
According to Mr. Kim from the store,

98
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:46,698
he's really good at  hwatu.

99
00:06:46,824 --> 00:06:48,283
-Really?
-Yes.

100
00:06:48,408 --> 00:06:51,036
I wonder what kind of trouble he caused.

101
00:06:51,161 --> 00:06:52,079
Exactly.

102
00:06:52,204 --> 00:06:54,331
-Maybe he was playing  hwatu  and--
-No way.

103
00:06:54,456 --> 00:06:55,290
Oh dear.

104
00:06:55,415 --> 00:06:57,751
-I got dumped by a girl.
-Oh!

105
00:07:00,045 --> 00:07:02,631
I got dumped by a girl
I liked for ten years,

106
00:07:03,423 --> 00:07:04,842
so I ran away.

107
00:07:05,384 --> 00:07:06,802
-Ran away?
-Ran away?

108
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:09,638
Yes, it hurt too much to keep seeing her.

109
00:07:09,763 --> 00:07:13,225
So I ran as far away as possible.

110
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:14,935
First, a month in Chungju,

111
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:17,020
then Daejeon,

112
00:07:17,813 --> 00:07:20,023
Suncheon, Namwon, and Boseong.

113
00:07:20,149 --> 00:07:24,361
And before I knew it,
I made it to the edge of the land.

114
00:07:28,157 --> 00:07:28,991
Back to work.

115
00:07:29,116 --> 00:07:30,159
-Right.
-Oh my.

116
00:07:30,284 --> 00:07:31,994
-My, my.
-Grab here.

117
00:07:32,119 --> 00:07:34,121
-Gosh.
-Grab it.

118
00:07:34,246 --> 00:07:35,497
Oh my.

119
00:07:35,622 --> 00:07:39,418
How long is she going to
be like that, anyway?

120
00:07:44,715 --> 00:07:46,049
Connect the TV.

121
00:07:46,758 --> 00:07:48,594
I need to watch the news.

122
00:07:48,719 --> 00:07:50,220
I said no.

123
00:07:50,345 --> 00:07:51,388
Stop.

124
00:07:51,513 --> 00:07:52,848
It's not because of Dad.

125
00:07:52,973 --> 00:07:54,850
I need to prepare my article portfolio

126
00:07:54,975 --> 00:07:57,186
for the youth journalism contest
in September.

127
00:07:57,311 --> 00:07:59,146
Hey, Deok-sun.

128
00:07:59,271 --> 00:08:03,108
Your aunt is doing this
because she's worried about you.

129
00:08:03,233 --> 00:08:05,611
Your father, Yong-dae, told us

130
00:08:05,736 --> 00:08:10,115
not to let you watch the news.
He practically begged us.

131
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:13,035
He deserves to be criticized
for disgracing the national uniform.

132
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:15,454
-Goodness!
-My dad is just paying the price

133
00:08:15,579 --> 00:08:17,497
for his negative impact on society.

134
00:08:17,623 --> 00:08:19,458
-That little--
-Oh, no.

135
00:08:19,583 --> 00:08:20,918
-Calm down.
-Calm down.

136
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:23,170
Are you not going to turn it on?

137
00:08:24,296 --> 00:08:26,173
Fine, I'll take care of it.

138
00:08:26,298 --> 00:08:27,633
-Hey!
-That brat.

139
00:08:27,758 --> 00:08:28,592
Oh my goodness.

140
00:08:28,717 --> 00:08:31,094
I'll make you eat seaweed soup
so you lose the contest!

141
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:32,221
You're dead meat!

142
00:08:32,346 --> 00:08:34,223
We also can't watch TV because of her.

143
00:08:34,348 --> 00:08:36,433
Get to work.

144
00:08:36,558 --> 00:08:37,809
Get over here!

145
00:08:38,435 --> 00:08:39,519
How upsetting.

146
00:08:45,817 --> 00:08:47,069
Damn it.

147
00:08:55,577 --> 00:08:56,411
Oh!

148
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:57,412
SU-YEON

149
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:06,755
DAD

150
00:09:08,674 --> 00:09:10,008
I lied.

151
00:09:10,133 --> 00:09:11,635
I didn't post it.

152
00:09:16,598 --> 00:09:17,474
What?

153
00:09:20,435 --> 00:09:21,270
Please.

154
00:09:37,995 --> 00:09:39,955
This is so annoying.

155
00:09:54,011 --> 00:09:55,095
What are you doing?

156
00:09:56,847 --> 00:09:58,515
How long have you been there?

157
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:02,269
Since you started bawling like, "Waah!"

158
00:10:03,437 --> 00:10:05,105
I don't cry like that.

159
00:10:05,772 --> 00:10:06,732
If you say so.

160
00:10:18,452 --> 00:10:19,786
What, you want one?

161
00:10:21,330 --> 00:10:23,874
I'm in high school. That's bad.

162
00:10:23,999 --> 00:10:26,918
What you did to your dad's mural is bad.

163
00:10:30,047 --> 00:10:31,631
This is just…

164
00:10:33,759 --> 00:10:36,303
a 225-won comfort.

165
00:10:42,976 --> 00:10:43,977
Let me have one.

166
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:50,400
That 225-won comfort.

167
00:11:37,114 --> 00:11:38,907
Hey, Deok-sun.

168
00:11:39,032 --> 00:11:40,200
Look at you now.

169
00:11:44,037 --> 00:11:46,164
What are you doing? Sit.

170
00:12:02,305 --> 00:12:04,641
It was funny
how you pretended not to know me,

171
00:12:04,766 --> 00:12:06,268
so I played along.

172
00:12:06,393 --> 00:12:08,520
But you never stopped pretending.

173
00:12:09,354 --> 00:12:10,897
Were you going to keep pretending?

174
00:12:11,022 --> 00:12:12,607
-Yes.
-"Yes"?

175
00:12:12,732 --> 00:12:16,653
A lot of time has passed,
and the workplace is a professional space.

176
00:12:16,778 --> 00:12:18,238
And more importantly,

177
00:12:18,363 --> 00:12:20,449
since we were never that close anyway,

178
00:12:21,533 --> 00:12:24,286
I didn't think
there was any need to acknowledge you.

179
00:12:27,956 --> 00:12:30,959
Then you should've kept it up.
Why did you suddenly show up?

180
00:12:33,837 --> 00:12:36,715
I needed the sample processing date.

181
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:37,841
And back then,

182
00:12:38,508 --> 00:12:41,136
I didn't know
you were a selfish bystander.

183
00:12:41,261 --> 00:12:43,388
-"A bystander"?
-Let me ask you something.

184
00:12:43,513 --> 00:12:45,348
Why I got in Mr. Oh's truck,

185
00:12:45,474 --> 00:12:47,559
and why my sudden interest
in the sweet potatoes?

186
00:12:47,684 --> 00:12:49,644
Is that what you want to know?

187
00:12:56,693 --> 00:12:59,070
How many quarterly
subcontractor goods receipts do you have?

188
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:03,950
I've secured up to the third quarter.

189
00:13:06,369 --> 00:13:07,787
Secure all of last year's first.

190
00:13:12,959 --> 00:13:14,336
Eat up.

191
00:13:14,461 --> 00:13:16,588
Traffic will be bad later.
We can't make any stops.

192
00:14:03,677 --> 00:14:05,011
I'm so sorry.

193
00:14:26,366 --> 00:14:28,410
I thought it was all discarded.

194
00:14:29,035 --> 00:14:30,829
Why do something different for no reason?

195
00:14:30,954 --> 00:14:33,290
This wouldn't have happened
with our usual supplier.

196
00:14:33,415 --> 00:14:36,376
He was just trying his best
to lower the unit cost.

197
00:14:36,501 --> 00:14:39,462
Why did he need to try?
No one cares anyway.

198
00:14:39,588 --> 00:14:43,133
But there were no issues
with the vacuum sealing during testing.

199
00:14:44,342 --> 00:14:46,845
They probably ran it
with the laminated film spec then,

200
00:14:47,387 --> 00:14:48,680
but changed it for production.

201
00:14:48,805 --> 00:14:52,350
Why let yourself get ripped off like that?

202
00:14:52,475 --> 00:14:53,935
He started when you did, right?

203
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:58,064
Anyway, try not to stand out or act up.

204
00:14:58,189 --> 00:15:00,108
Especially you, Gung.

205
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:01,776
Don't get cocky, got it?

206
00:15:02,444 --> 00:15:04,613
Of course,
I'll listen to your expert advice.

207
00:15:04,738 --> 00:15:05,780
I won't forget.

208
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:07,866
Why, you little…

209
00:15:07,991 --> 00:15:09,659
I have plans. Have lunch without me.

210
00:15:09,784 --> 00:15:11,536
Oh, take Ms. Park Su-a with you.

211
00:15:11,661 --> 00:15:13,163
-Take her.
-I will.

212
00:15:13,288 --> 00:15:14,539
Why doesn't he take her?

213
00:15:15,707 --> 00:15:17,542
Eat up, Yeon-ju.

214
00:15:18,501 --> 00:15:19,502
Fill yourself.

215
00:15:19,628 --> 00:15:20,712
Just spit it out.

216
00:15:20,837 --> 00:15:23,798
After I see you eat
ten pieces of meat first.

217
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:25,467
I'm not that antisocial.

218
00:15:26,426 --> 00:15:28,094
Mi-do refuses to sign the agreement.

219
00:15:28,219 --> 00:15:30,013
It's really stressing me out.

220
00:15:35,685 --> 00:15:36,770
It's dragging on.

221
00:15:37,437 --> 00:15:38,647
You need to persuade her.

222
00:15:38,772 --> 00:15:40,982
This will hit the news and go to trial.

223
00:15:41,107 --> 00:15:42,192
Then so be it.

224
00:15:42,317 --> 00:15:44,235
Are you crazy? You have to stop her.

225
00:15:44,361 --> 00:15:45,904
Mi-do is out of her mind.

226
00:15:46,905 --> 00:15:48,865
Do you know how bad the situation is?

227
00:15:50,158 --> 00:15:52,285
If she's doing this despite that,

228
00:15:52,410 --> 00:15:54,162
she must have a good reason.

229
00:15:54,287 --> 00:15:56,039
She can be a bit too emotional,

230
00:15:56,706 --> 00:15:59,542
but when it comes to films,
she has strong convictions

231
00:16:00,669 --> 00:16:01,753
or values.

232
00:16:02,295 --> 00:16:03,797
She's very firm about them.

233
00:16:04,673 --> 00:16:05,715
And I respect that.

234
00:16:08,218 --> 00:16:09,552
So, about that.

235
00:16:11,596 --> 00:16:13,765
How much does it cost to go to trial?

236
00:16:13,890 --> 00:16:15,684
I have some savings accounts
maturing soon.

237
00:16:16,309 --> 00:16:17,894
Thirty…

238
00:16:18,019 --> 00:16:19,020
Is it expensive?

239
00:16:23,024 --> 00:16:26,027
Maybe Mi-do just isn't cut out
for commercial films.

240
00:16:26,152 --> 00:16:28,530
The "rising director" label
is no longer good for her.

241
00:16:28,655 --> 00:16:32,367
Aside from the trial,
Mi-do is at a point in her career

242
00:16:32,492 --> 00:16:35,370
where she needs to decide
which path to take.

243
00:16:39,749 --> 00:16:44,170
The ceiling is seven meters high,
and the aisle is about 20 meters long.

244
00:16:44,295 --> 00:16:48,091
The lighting is designed
to complement the bride's figure,

245
00:16:48,216 --> 00:16:51,052
so brides are very satisfied with it.

246
00:17:02,564 --> 00:17:03,398
Um…

247
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:07,777
We'll only have about 200 guests,
so this feels a bit too spacious.

248
00:17:07,902 --> 00:17:09,112
Any other halls?

249
00:17:09,237 --> 00:17:11,239
Oh, just a moment.

250
00:17:14,951 --> 00:17:17,078
NAMGUNG, MI-DO
YEONHWARU

251
00:17:19,289 --> 00:17:20,665
The first one was best,

252
00:17:21,499 --> 00:17:22,667
but ten is too early.

253
00:17:22,792 --> 00:17:24,627
Your relatives are coming from Yangyang.

254
00:17:24,753 --> 00:17:26,504
I'm not inviting my relatives.

255
00:17:28,423 --> 00:17:32,177
I don't want empty congratulations
from people I rarely even see.

256
00:17:33,178 --> 00:17:36,473
Anyway, they already gave cash gifts
when Yeong-do got married.

257
00:17:36,598 --> 00:17:38,224
I'm sure Mom will be fine.

258
00:17:40,769 --> 00:17:41,895
What?

259
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:45,356
Midori, don't try to be considerate.
It's not like you.

260
00:17:46,941 --> 00:17:49,402
-What do you mean?
-I know you're doing it for me.

261
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:52,363
Since when are you so selfless?
It's weirding me out.

262
00:17:52,489 --> 00:17:53,990
You've got it wrong.

263
00:17:54,115 --> 00:17:57,619
I just don't want to invite relatives
because I'm a mess right now.

264
00:17:57,744 --> 00:17:58,703
It's not for you.

265
00:18:13,134 --> 00:18:13,968
Open it.

266
00:18:14,803 --> 00:18:15,637
What is it?

267
00:18:21,226 --> 00:18:22,644
FILM PRODUCTION GRANT APPLICATION

268
00:18:22,769 --> 00:18:24,604
I checked, and you qualify.

269
00:18:24,729 --> 00:18:26,481
You said the script you're writing

270
00:18:26,606 --> 00:18:29,192
isn't big enough in scale
to be a commercial film.

271
00:18:30,568 --> 00:18:33,071
They cover up to 80%
of the production costs,

272
00:18:33,196 --> 00:18:34,823
and I'll invest the rest.

273
00:18:36,950 --> 00:18:38,743
Here, one more thing.

274
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:43,414
INSTALLMENT SAVINGS ACCOUNT

275
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:45,250
This account matures next month.

276
00:18:45,375 --> 00:18:46,793
I work for a good company

277
00:18:46,918 --> 00:18:49,379
that offers a housing deposit loan
as an employee benefit.

278
00:18:49,504 --> 00:18:51,673
So I'm going to invest this in you.

279
00:18:53,591 --> 00:18:55,969
No, why would I accept this?

280
00:19:00,014 --> 00:19:00,974
Mi-do.

281
00:19:02,767 --> 00:19:05,103
I sometimes regret
quitting art like I did.

282
00:19:13,236 --> 00:19:15,864
YEONUL HIGH SCHOOL
IT STARTS WITH SMALL ACTIONS

283
00:19:20,451 --> 00:19:21,327
Namgung!

284
00:19:22,203 --> 00:19:23,162
Namgung!

285
00:19:24,747 --> 00:19:26,624
Namgung! Let go!

286
00:19:26,749 --> 00:19:28,960
Are you crazy? Namgung!

287
00:19:30,211 --> 00:19:31,170
Let go.

288
00:19:31,296 --> 00:19:32,714
Are you sure you got everything?

289
00:19:32,839 --> 00:19:35,925
I searched Mom's room and hers
and brought everything.

290
00:19:36,509 --> 00:19:38,344
Why? Is something missing?

291
00:19:42,765 --> 00:19:43,683
Where is it?

292
00:19:45,476 --> 00:19:48,563
Where's the drawing I did for you
at the picnic this spring?

293
00:19:52,775 --> 00:19:54,027
It's mine.

294
00:19:55,111 --> 00:19:56,779
You drew it, but it's mine.

295
00:20:01,117 --> 00:20:01,951
Hey.

296
00:20:02,744 --> 00:20:04,162
What are you…

297
00:20:05,371 --> 00:20:07,624
No, don't!

298
00:20:08,333 --> 00:20:10,209
Hey, no!

299
00:20:10,335 --> 00:20:12,086
-Stop.
-Let go.

300
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:13,463
No, don't!

301
00:20:14,714 --> 00:20:15,632
No!

302
00:20:16,299 --> 00:20:17,675
Hey, don't do it.

303
00:20:19,385 --> 00:20:20,303
No.

304
00:20:20,428 --> 00:20:22,430
No, no!

305
00:20:22,555 --> 00:20:24,098
No!

306
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,457
Do you have to do this?

307
00:20:50,375 --> 00:20:51,793
Do you really have to…

308
00:20:51,918 --> 00:20:55,588
You're the one hurting more.

309
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:58,675
Why are you doing this to yourself?

310
00:20:59,509 --> 00:21:00,551
It's really…

311
00:21:01,761 --> 00:21:03,137
over.

312
00:21:05,348 --> 00:21:07,475
It's really, really…

313
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:10,645
over.

314
00:21:18,361 --> 00:21:20,989
I don't know why
I was so extreme back then.

315
00:21:22,615 --> 00:21:25,076
As if keeping one drawing was a huge deal.

316
00:21:26,369 --> 00:21:27,203
Funny, right?

317
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:28,746
No.

318
00:21:30,665 --> 00:21:31,791
It's not funny at all.

319
00:21:36,254 --> 00:21:37,130
Are you mad?

320
00:21:37,672 --> 00:21:38,548
Namgung.

321
00:21:39,257 --> 00:21:41,217
Do you want to draw again?

322
00:21:46,597 --> 00:21:47,932
I just…

323
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:50,560
never saw it through,

324
00:21:51,811 --> 00:21:53,312
so I think about it sometimes.

325
00:21:53,438 --> 00:21:55,648
-You said you regret it.
-Yes.

326
00:21:56,774 --> 00:21:59,193
So I don't want you to end up like me.

327
00:22:01,571 --> 00:22:03,865
Don't let your circumstances

328
00:22:04,949 --> 00:22:07,076
make you give up what you love.

329
00:22:09,037 --> 00:22:10,455
Do what you enjoy

330
00:22:11,581 --> 00:22:13,583
for the rest of your life.

331
00:22:14,584 --> 00:22:15,793
That suits you.

332
00:22:20,089 --> 00:22:21,174
I'm starving.

333
00:22:24,719 --> 00:22:25,845
-Eat up.
-Okay.

334
00:22:38,524 --> 00:22:40,318
-Midori.
-Yes?

335
00:22:41,444 --> 00:22:42,445
Open the glove box.

336
00:23:06,094 --> 00:23:08,471
The theaters are all booked this year.

337
00:23:11,766 --> 00:23:15,019
You always dreamed of
getting proposed to at Seoul Art Cinema.

338
00:23:17,772 --> 00:23:20,274
I actually had everything
planned out last time.

339
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:22,360
What?

340
00:23:22,485 --> 00:23:24,070
I couldn't put it off anymore.

341
00:23:24,195 --> 00:23:25,696
Let's keep it simple today,

342
00:23:26,322 --> 00:23:28,449
and I'll redo it at the theater next year.

343
00:23:29,325 --> 00:23:31,577
You better act surprised
even if you already know.

344
00:23:35,998 --> 00:23:37,500
Hey, Sister Lee.

345
00:23:37,625 --> 00:23:39,710
Shouldn't you act more touched right now?

346
00:23:39,836 --> 00:23:41,254
Or shed some tears?

347
00:23:41,379 --> 00:23:43,965
How much longer
are you going to be so down?

348
00:23:44,090 --> 00:23:45,925
Just give me a second, then.

349
00:23:54,225 --> 00:23:57,311
Shouldn't we at least hug?

350
00:23:58,312 --> 00:23:59,480
Right. Come here.

351
00:24:00,398 --> 00:24:01,732
There we go.

352
00:24:04,318 --> 00:24:05,778
-And kiss?
-I guess so.

353
00:24:05,903 --> 00:24:06,779
Hold on.

354
00:24:07,488 --> 00:24:08,489
-Coming.
-Okay.

355
00:24:10,825 --> 00:24:12,243
-Let's do it at home.
-Yeah.

356
00:24:13,452 --> 00:24:14,370
I'm sorry.

357
00:24:37,685 --> 00:24:40,563
Nobu Film met
Director Kim Jung-man yesterday.

358
00:24:40,688 --> 00:24:42,899
What should we do? Start working?

359
00:24:43,024 --> 00:24:44,483
This bastard!

360
00:24:53,284 --> 00:24:54,827
25TH

361
00:24:54,994 --> 00:24:57,622
ANY SPARE MONEY?
I NEED TWO MILLION WON MORE THIS MONTH.

362
00:25:41,749 --> 00:25:43,167
SIM HAE-JU

363
00:25:48,256 --> 00:25:50,299
I think Director Lee is dead.

364
00:25:50,424 --> 00:25:51,467
Check if she's alive.

365
00:25:52,260 --> 00:25:53,469
Just a moment.

366
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:57,515
Her last social media login
was four minutes ago.

367
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:59,517
The IP is from her usual coffee shop.

368
00:25:59,642 --> 00:26:01,060
So she is alive!

369
00:26:03,145 --> 00:26:05,273
But she's been ignoring
all my calls and texts.

370
00:26:07,566 --> 00:26:08,651
Unbelievable.

371
00:26:10,486 --> 00:26:12,321
Send me her location. No, wait.

372
00:26:12,446 --> 00:26:14,156
Send her location in 15 minutes.

373
00:26:15,074 --> 00:26:16,784
What? How am I supposed to--

374
00:26:26,877 --> 00:26:28,212
Seriously.

375
00:26:28,337 --> 00:26:30,131
She must be at her usual coffee shop.

376
00:26:30,256 --> 00:26:31,924
She used her card eight minutes ago.

377
00:26:32,049 --> 00:26:33,301
You know the address, right?

378
00:26:40,224 --> 00:26:41,142
Hey.

379
00:26:45,855 --> 00:26:49,317
Lawyers talk too much,
whether in the US or Korea.

380
00:26:49,442 --> 00:26:52,445
They called it a conference,
but it was practically a debate.

381
00:26:52,570 --> 00:26:55,656
I barely made my flight, too.

382
00:26:55,781 --> 00:26:58,034
If I missed it, I'd be divorced.

383
00:26:58,993 --> 00:27:01,495
Assemblyman Kang's
book launch was today, right?

384
00:27:01,620 --> 00:27:03,998
My father-in-law… What was it last time?

385
00:27:04,123 --> 00:27:06,000
Hanmaeum or Saemaeum?

386
00:27:06,125 --> 00:27:07,293
Anyway,

387
00:27:07,418 --> 00:27:10,129
he was so mad
I missed the party members' sports day.

388
00:27:10,254 --> 00:27:13,257
I just showed my face
and used the trial as an excuse to leave.

389
00:27:13,924 --> 00:27:16,052
Did you see my email? About Jisang.

390
00:27:16,177 --> 00:27:18,304
Yes, I saw it.

391
00:27:18,429 --> 00:27:22,183
The evidence of tech similarity
that Line submitted is too solid.

392
00:27:22,308 --> 00:27:24,477
The patent infringement is undeniable.

393
00:27:24,602 --> 00:27:28,105
Unless something changes,
Jisang has no chance of winning.

394
00:27:29,315 --> 00:27:30,775
I suggest you don't take it.

395
00:27:30,900 --> 00:27:32,068
Really?

396
00:27:33,319 --> 00:27:34,737
You think we'd lose?

397
00:27:34,862 --> 00:27:36,489
Based on the current evidence,

398
00:27:37,323 --> 00:27:39,909
yes, I think so.

399
00:27:40,576 --> 00:27:41,827
That's great.

400
00:27:43,954 --> 00:27:44,872
Lose the case.

401
00:27:58,052 --> 00:28:00,221
Jisang's Chairman Ko and Assemblyman Shin

402
00:28:00,346 --> 00:28:02,139
are clashing over the land in Daewon-dong.

403
00:28:02,890 --> 00:28:06,394
If Jisang loses,
they'll need the settlement money.

404
00:28:07,228 --> 00:28:09,271
So they'll sell the land.

405
00:28:13,734 --> 00:28:17,029
Make it as flashy as possible,

406
00:28:17,863 --> 00:28:19,115
and lose the case.

407
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:20,699
You can do that, right?

408
00:28:25,871 --> 00:28:27,832
DIRECTOR LEE MI-DO

409
00:28:35,047 --> 00:28:36,132
Come back as a director?

410
00:28:36,257 --> 00:28:38,509
What? Can you not handle it?

411
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:40,803
You said you could.

412
00:28:42,888 --> 00:28:44,348
I'm curious

413
00:28:44,473 --> 00:28:46,851
why you changed your mind
in just a few days.

414
00:28:48,894 --> 00:28:50,479
There must be something

415
00:28:51,439 --> 00:28:52,606
that you're hiding.

416
00:28:53,232 --> 00:28:55,109
Is that your way of saying no?

417
00:28:55,234 --> 00:28:56,444
Is it your boyfriend again?

418
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:02,324
I knew it. It is.

419
00:29:02,450 --> 00:29:03,576
What is it?

420
00:29:03,701 --> 00:29:06,203
He won't marry you
unless you're a director?

421
00:29:06,328 --> 00:29:07,538
Did he say no?

422
00:29:07,663 --> 00:29:08,831
Not him. Me.

423
00:29:10,499 --> 00:29:11,959
I say no.

424
00:29:14,712 --> 00:29:16,922
I'd be a burden to him like this.

425
00:29:17,548 --> 00:29:18,716
I'm saying no to that.

426
00:29:20,468 --> 00:29:22,052
So I'm compromising.

427
00:29:30,060 --> 00:29:32,021
I'll get the other candidates
out of your way,

428
00:29:32,146 --> 00:29:34,231
but your history with Ms. Song?

429
00:29:34,356 --> 00:29:35,774
You have to resolve that.

430
00:29:35,900 --> 00:29:37,234
I know.

431
00:29:37,359 --> 00:29:40,946
If we use her affair with Mr. Seo,
we could persuade her for now--

432
00:29:41,071 --> 00:29:42,490
No, I don't want that.

433
00:29:42,615 --> 00:29:43,866
Neither do I.

434
00:29:44,950 --> 00:29:47,077
Don't give her the upper hand.

435
00:29:51,832 --> 00:29:54,043
Ms. Song
is at her Gapyeong house right now.

436
00:29:55,753 --> 00:29:58,130
I'll let her know you're coming.

437
00:29:58,797 --> 00:30:00,841
Go there and do whatever you can,

438
00:30:00,966 --> 00:30:02,676
whether it's begging or pleading.

439
00:30:04,512 --> 00:30:06,388
I'm making this clear.

440
00:30:07,640 --> 00:30:09,892
Persuading Ms. Song is your job.

441
00:30:29,370 --> 00:30:30,454
You're early.

442
00:30:30,579 --> 00:30:32,414
Oh, yes.

443
00:30:32,540 --> 00:30:34,250
Are you prepared?

444
00:30:35,042 --> 00:30:37,586
To deal with someone so difficult.

445
00:30:39,255 --> 00:30:40,923
There might be yelling

446
00:30:41,048 --> 00:30:43,008
or even violence.

447
00:30:45,844 --> 00:30:49,390
I'll try to talk things out
so that won't happen.

448
00:30:50,724 --> 00:30:52,601
With some people, that's impossible.

449
00:30:53,269 --> 00:30:55,145
I know, but still.

450
00:30:55,271 --> 00:30:57,481
With someone
who can't even use the bathroom alone?

451
00:30:57,606 --> 00:30:58,649
It'll be hard.

452
00:31:00,276 --> 00:31:01,318
By the way,

453
00:31:02,152 --> 00:31:03,654
you have experience, right?

454
00:31:03,779 --> 00:31:05,364
You just look so young.

455
00:31:05,948 --> 00:31:09,076
I'm sorry, is this an interview?

456
00:31:10,286 --> 00:31:12,746
Aren't you here
for the 3 p.m. caregiver interview?

457
00:31:12,871 --> 00:31:15,416
No, I'm actually here
to see Ms. Song Hae-na.

458
00:31:18,502 --> 00:31:20,379
Are you a reporter, by any chance?

459
00:31:20,504 --> 00:31:23,007
No, I'm not a reporter…

460
00:31:24,300 --> 00:31:25,884
Hae-na?

461
00:31:42,610 --> 00:31:44,486
THE EMPEROR'S BLUEPRINT

462
00:31:45,571 --> 00:31:46,447
What is this?

463
00:31:46,572 --> 00:31:49,199
I prepared a Plan B just in case.

464
00:31:50,701 --> 00:31:53,287
It's a movie K4 Pictures is preparing.
It's based on a true story.

465
00:31:53,412 --> 00:31:54,663
THE CONFESSION OF THE ULTIMATE FRAUDSTER,
SONG GI-PAL

466
00:31:54,788 --> 00:31:58,250
I've set it up
so you can direct this movie.

467
00:31:59,418 --> 00:32:00,377
This guy…

468
00:32:00,502 --> 00:32:01,629
That's right.

469
00:32:02,588 --> 00:32:04,673
30,000 victims
and 50 billion won in damages at the time.

470
00:32:04,798 --> 00:32:06,383
ATTRACTED INVESTORS
BY PROMISING HIGH RETURNS

471
00:32:06,508 --> 00:32:09,094
He ran Korea's first mega-Ponzi scheme.

472
00:32:09,803 --> 00:32:12,139
Song Gi-pal, the real estate scammer.

473
00:32:22,816 --> 00:32:25,611
It was my second year with the company.

474
00:32:25,736 --> 00:32:28,906
The O-SweeTato Chips started sticking
in the final process…

475
00:32:29,031 --> 00:32:31,158
Mr. Namgung. Are you coming?

476
00:32:31,283 --> 00:32:34,662
The moisture variance was so bad
that the whole line almost stopped.

477
00:32:35,245 --> 00:32:38,457
That's when I figured it out.

478
00:32:38,582 --> 00:32:40,668
It was the temperature
and discharge speed.

479
00:32:40,793 --> 00:32:44,672
And thanks to that, you were the first
among your fellow hires to get promoted.

480
00:32:44,797 --> 00:32:47,174
-You need to be more precise.
-I think I know

481
00:32:47,299 --> 00:32:48,759
why you told me to secure

482
00:32:48,884 --> 00:32:50,969
all of last year's
subcontractor goods receipts.

483
00:32:51,095 --> 00:32:52,971
Come on, Assistant Manager Gung
broke that.

484
00:32:53,097 --> 00:32:54,973
Now, it was my fourth year.

485
00:32:55,099 --> 00:32:56,892
Out of all my peers

486
00:32:57,017 --> 00:32:58,852
-and seniors…
-Where are we now?

487
00:32:58,977 --> 00:33:02,189
Year four, the history
of his challenges and hardships.

488
00:33:02,314 --> 00:33:03,399
Yes, right.

489
00:33:04,149 --> 00:33:05,442
Hey, are you even listening?

490
00:33:05,567 --> 00:33:07,027
We're all listening.

491
00:33:07,152 --> 00:33:08,612
Kang's scheme ruined the survey.

492
00:33:08,737 --> 00:33:11,240
Then? I'm dying to know
even though I've heard it before.

493
00:33:11,365 --> 00:33:12,533
Right?

494
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:14,493
-Out of all--
-Cheers.

495
00:33:14,618 --> 00:33:16,161
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

496
00:33:19,498 --> 00:33:21,583
Scheming to plot and rule.

497
00:33:21,709 --> 00:33:23,502
-Grill some kimchi.
-Put some kimchi on.

498
00:33:23,627 --> 00:33:24,920
-Right now?
-Yes.

499
00:33:25,045 --> 00:33:26,880
-Want some garlic?
-Yes, please.

500
00:33:27,548 --> 00:33:29,007
I'll check right away.

501
00:33:42,855 --> 00:33:43,939
Jeez!

502
00:33:44,982 --> 00:33:45,983
You scared me.

503
00:33:48,068 --> 00:33:50,821
You're looking for volume mismatches
and the tipping point.

504
00:33:50,946 --> 00:33:51,989
Right? Aren't you?

505
00:33:53,949 --> 00:33:55,701
Please, tell me. Am I right?

506
00:33:56,660 --> 00:33:58,620
-Yes, you are.
-Yes!

507
00:33:58,746 --> 00:34:00,748
Right on! Yes!

508
00:34:07,838 --> 00:34:08,714
Well…

509
00:34:08,839 --> 00:34:11,300
It's exactly as I thought.

510
00:34:12,217 --> 00:34:13,594
Checking the farm shipment records,

511
00:34:13,719 --> 00:34:16,263
the unit price curve
drops at a weird point,

512
00:34:16,388 --> 00:34:17,723
so it's a volume issue.

513
00:34:21,977 --> 00:34:25,898
Anyway, why didn't you text me back?

514
00:34:26,023 --> 00:34:29,067
If I didn't know you were busy,
I'd think you ignored me.

515
00:34:29,193 --> 00:34:30,986
I almost took it the wrong way.

516
00:34:31,111 --> 00:34:33,030
I did ignore you on purpose.

517
00:34:33,155 --> 00:34:35,616
Right? I thought you were ignoring…

518
00:34:36,533 --> 00:34:37,409
What?

519
00:34:38,744 --> 00:34:39,787
I thought it'd be

520
00:34:39,912 --> 00:34:42,873
more polite to tell you in person.

521
00:34:46,001 --> 00:34:47,753
I don't think I can do it.

522
00:34:48,462 --> 00:34:50,464
What? Why all of a sudden…

523
00:34:56,386 --> 00:34:57,513
Can I…

524
00:34:58,847 --> 00:34:59,890
ask you why?

525
00:35:01,225 --> 00:35:02,392
I just…

526
00:35:04,061 --> 00:35:06,021
suddenly lost interest.

527
00:35:08,440 --> 00:35:09,942
That's a lie.

528
00:35:10,067 --> 00:35:12,277
Honestly, I was motivated that day.

529
00:35:12,402 --> 00:35:14,404
I was fired up with a sense of justice.

530
00:35:16,907 --> 00:35:18,617
But after thinking about it…

531
00:35:22,704 --> 00:35:24,122
I got scared.

532
00:35:26,750 --> 00:35:28,961
Life isn't like dramas.

533
00:35:31,880 --> 00:35:33,131
It's not  Hanzawa Naoki.

534
00:35:37,427 --> 00:35:39,179
Do you know what my dream is?

535
00:35:40,848 --> 00:35:44,101
To hold out as General Manager
until I'm 60,

536
00:35:44,226 --> 00:35:45,769
and then retire.

537
00:35:48,272 --> 00:35:50,983
Pretty pathetic and lame, right?

538
00:35:53,610 --> 00:35:54,611
But…

539
00:35:55,946 --> 00:35:57,197
that's my dream.

540
00:35:59,992 --> 00:36:02,452
So stop trying to sway me.

541
00:36:03,537 --> 00:36:04,663
Kiddo!

542
00:36:25,851 --> 00:36:27,477
Put it on my card.

543
00:36:27,603 --> 00:36:29,563
-It is your card.
-Oh, is it?

544
00:36:29,688 --> 00:36:30,814
-Yes, sir.
-Okay.

545
00:36:30,939 --> 00:36:32,065
-Thanks.
-Thank you.

546
00:36:32,190 --> 00:36:33,984
-You're welcome. Take care.
-You too.

547
00:36:34,610 --> 00:36:36,278
-I called a cab.
-Okay.

548
00:36:36,403 --> 00:36:37,779
I'll take Manager Eom home.

549
00:36:37,905 --> 00:36:39,656
-And Ms. Park?
-She's in the restroom.

550
00:36:39,781 --> 00:36:41,867
Manager Eom spilled stew on her.

551
00:36:41,992 --> 00:36:43,702
Hold on, we'll head out first.

552
00:36:43,827 --> 00:36:45,329
-All right.
-Take care.

553
00:36:45,996 --> 00:36:47,539
Yes, sir.

554
00:36:47,664 --> 00:36:49,958
Yes, that's right. It's the Mercedes.

555
00:36:51,376 --> 00:36:53,921
Yes, I'll head over there now.

556
00:36:54,838 --> 00:36:56,590
Come on, get closer.

557
00:36:56,715 --> 00:36:58,091
It's cold.

558
00:36:59,635 --> 00:37:00,886
RESTROOM

559
00:37:01,887 --> 00:37:03,555
Su-a, are you in there?

560
00:37:10,270 --> 00:37:13,440
The stain on my clothes isn't coming out.

561
00:37:13,565 --> 00:37:14,483
You can go ahead.

562
00:37:14,608 --> 00:37:16,026
It's fine. I'll wait.

563
00:37:21,031 --> 00:37:22,240
Will you be long?

564
00:37:25,744 --> 00:37:28,538
I'm fine, really! You can go!

565
00:37:29,456 --> 00:37:30,540
Are you sure?

566
00:37:31,083 --> 00:37:32,167
I'm leaving, then.

567
00:37:43,136 --> 00:37:44,513
Why do you sound like that?

568
00:37:47,599 --> 00:37:48,600
Su-a.

569
00:38:02,406 --> 00:38:05,325
There's only one key. What should we do?

570
00:38:06,118 --> 00:38:08,537
-Call the police first.
-Okay.

571
00:38:17,379 --> 00:38:18,922
You want to see her die?

572
00:38:19,047 --> 00:38:20,465
I have a knife!

573
00:38:21,925 --> 00:38:23,093
So what?

574
00:38:23,844 --> 00:38:25,012
I'll kill you first.

575
00:38:32,644 --> 00:38:33,520
Don't come closer!

576
00:38:34,479 --> 00:38:36,857
She's really going to die.
I'm not messing around.

577
00:38:36,982 --> 00:38:37,899
I'll stab her.

578
00:38:41,236 --> 00:38:42,279
Hey.

579
00:38:42,863 --> 00:38:44,906
The police will be here in two minutes.

580
00:38:45,032 --> 00:38:47,909
If you drop the knife and leave right now,

581
00:38:48,035 --> 00:38:49,244
I won't come after you.

582
00:38:51,038 --> 00:38:51,872
But…

583
00:38:52,664 --> 00:38:54,332
if you try anything stupid?

584
00:38:55,417 --> 00:38:56,334
Then you're dead.

585
00:38:57,961 --> 00:38:59,296
What's it going to be?

586
00:39:00,255 --> 00:39:01,631
We don't have time. Decide fast.

587
00:39:01,757 --> 00:39:03,592
Bullshit! How can I trust you?

588
00:39:04,926 --> 00:39:05,927
One minute left.

589
00:39:07,763 --> 00:39:09,181
The police are coming.

590
00:39:24,821 --> 00:39:25,947
Are you okay?

591
00:39:29,618 --> 00:39:30,786
Stay here for a second.

592
00:39:30,911 --> 00:39:32,037
No!

593
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:35,791
He has a knife.

594
00:39:56,311 --> 00:39:57,979
Explain what happened.

595
00:40:03,443 --> 00:40:07,280
You said you wanted
to return to directing.

596
00:40:12,536 --> 00:40:15,413
That's why I gave you
a card to play against Song Hae-na.

597
00:40:15,539 --> 00:40:17,833
If that's what it is, I already have one.

598
00:40:17,958 --> 00:40:19,167
I know.

599
00:40:19,918 --> 00:40:22,587
But using that
would be exhausting for both of us.

600
00:40:22,712 --> 00:40:24,965
That's why you haven't used it,

601
00:40:25,090 --> 00:40:26,508
and went to see her instead.

602
00:40:29,761 --> 00:40:31,304
Wow.

603
00:40:35,016 --> 00:40:36,268
What?

604
00:40:37,727 --> 00:40:40,021
Doubling the settlement is fine,

605
00:40:40,147 --> 00:40:42,190
but this weighs too heavily
on your conscience?

606
00:40:43,233 --> 00:40:44,526
Is that it?

607
00:40:45,652 --> 00:40:46,778
Oh well, then.

608
00:40:48,405 --> 00:40:50,282
I'll just have to do it for you.

609
00:40:59,749 --> 00:41:01,877
Hello, Ms. Song.

610
00:41:02,836 --> 00:41:06,089
Director Lee visited you
at your Gapyeong house today, right?

611
00:41:08,341 --> 00:41:10,594
It seems she heard it from Reporter Oh.

612
00:41:10,719 --> 00:41:12,804
She actually just came to see me

613
00:41:12,929 --> 00:41:15,098
and demanded her return as director.

614
00:41:20,353 --> 00:41:21,188
ACTRESS SONG HAE-NA

615
00:41:21,313 --> 00:41:22,480
What should we do?

616
00:41:24,733 --> 00:41:26,151
Tell her I'll give her anything.

617
00:41:27,569 --> 00:41:29,988
Her return, money, whatever.

618
00:41:31,239 --> 00:41:34,075
Tell her I'll give her
whatever she asks for.

619
00:41:35,744 --> 00:41:37,746
So please…

620
00:41:41,041 --> 00:41:42,584
Mr. Han.

621
00:41:42,709 --> 00:41:45,045
I'm sorry about last time.

622
00:41:45,170 --> 00:41:46,963
I'll never do that again.

623
00:41:48,840 --> 00:41:52,010
If this gets out, I'm dead.

624
00:41:52,135 --> 00:41:55,138
Do you know how hard I worked to get here?

625
00:41:59,226 --> 00:42:02,145
Of course, I know.

626
00:42:03,688 --> 00:42:07,525
You can't lose everything
because of your father.

627
00:42:08,235 --> 00:42:10,862
I really love acting.

628
00:42:10,987 --> 00:42:13,615
I love it so much.

629
00:42:14,366 --> 00:42:16,618
Stop crying, Ms. Song.

630
00:42:16,743 --> 00:42:18,828
Why are you crying over this?

631
00:42:20,163 --> 00:42:21,706
I'll take care of everything.

632
00:42:22,457 --> 00:42:26,211
Thank you so much, Mr. Han.

633
00:42:27,837 --> 00:42:30,507
First, I'll get in touch with Director Lee

634
00:42:30,632 --> 00:42:32,175
and call you back.

635
00:42:42,560 --> 00:42:43,979
Is this funny to you?

636
00:42:46,231 --> 00:42:47,732
I'm not a psychopath.

637
00:42:48,441 --> 00:42:51,361
I have my own struggles.

638
00:42:56,199 --> 00:42:57,158
You called, sir?

639
00:42:57,784 --> 00:42:58,952
Yes.

640
00:43:00,745 --> 00:43:04,165
Bring over a Ravello 4500

641
00:43:04,791 --> 00:43:06,793
and a fruit platter for her.

642
00:43:06,918 --> 00:43:09,462
Also, some sparkling water and ice.

643
00:43:09,587 --> 00:43:11,423
Make sure she has plenty.

644
00:43:11,548 --> 00:43:14,384
Yes, I'll prepare that right away, sir.

645
00:43:14,509 --> 00:43:15,427
Plenty.

646
00:43:22,058 --> 00:43:23,435
I'll give you two hours.

647
00:43:26,062 --> 00:43:27,814
I hope you take it seriously

648
00:43:28,356 --> 00:43:30,567
and make the right choice for yourself.

649
00:44:00,221 --> 00:44:02,140
What's wrong with you?

650
00:44:02,849 --> 00:44:04,392
What if I had just left?

651
00:44:05,769 --> 00:44:08,855
You should've screamed for help!
Are you stupid?

652
00:44:09,689 --> 00:44:11,066
What about you?

653
00:44:11,608 --> 00:44:12,942
You could've called the police.

654
00:44:13,068 --> 00:44:14,944
Why break the door and step in?

655
00:44:15,070 --> 00:44:17,906
You almost got hurt, too.
And you'd have blamed me for it!

656
00:44:18,031 --> 00:44:19,449
I'd thought it all out.

657
00:44:19,574 --> 00:44:21,368
I factored in the police ETA.

658
00:44:21,493 --> 00:44:23,536
Unlike you, I handle crises well.

659
00:44:23,661 --> 00:44:27,040
Oh, is that why
you went after someone who had a knife?

660
00:44:27,165 --> 00:44:27,999
I had him.

661
00:44:28,124 --> 00:44:30,502
You cost me the Civilian Heroism Award.

662
00:44:32,420 --> 00:44:34,130
How selfish of me! My apologies.

663
00:44:34,255 --> 00:44:35,757
-Hey!
-What?

664
00:44:36,424 --> 00:44:37,300
You…

665
00:44:42,013 --> 00:44:42,847
Are you hurt?

666
00:44:44,474 --> 00:44:45,809
Took you long enough.

667
00:44:46,434 --> 00:44:47,268
I'm fine.

668
00:44:47,394 --> 00:44:48,978
Are you traumatized at all?

669
00:44:49,104 --> 00:44:50,522
I don't think so, for now.

670
00:44:50,647 --> 00:44:51,856
Are you in shock?

671
00:44:51,981 --> 00:44:54,734
I was scared earlier, but I'm fine now.

672
00:44:54,859 --> 00:44:55,777
Need calming medicine?

673
00:44:57,320 --> 00:44:58,488
No, I don't.

674
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:03,701
Follow me.

675
00:45:06,704 --> 00:45:07,705
Come on!

676
00:45:10,125 --> 00:45:11,334
Where are we going?

677
00:45:11,459 --> 00:45:15,630
PRIME ON CONVENIENCE STORE

678
00:45:22,429 --> 00:45:23,304
I'm over these.

679
00:45:23,430 --> 00:45:24,264
NATURAL HONEY DRINK - BANANA MILK

680
00:45:24,389 --> 00:45:25,473
It's not for you.

681
00:45:36,985 --> 00:45:40,155
Your brain might deny it,
but you were definitely shaken up.

682
00:45:44,534 --> 00:45:45,952
I'm highly resilient.

683
00:45:46,703 --> 00:45:48,913
I took a test. I'm in the top 10%.

684
00:45:53,042 --> 00:45:56,421
Besides, I've been an outcast
since elementary school.

685
00:45:57,255 --> 00:45:58,339
I've been through worse.

686
00:45:58,465 --> 00:45:59,591
I've seen it all.

687
00:46:03,678 --> 00:46:05,054
Nothing too serious.

688
00:46:05,180 --> 00:46:06,848
My gym clothes got stolen,

689
00:46:06,973 --> 00:46:08,558
my textbooks were scribbled on…

690
00:46:08,683 --> 00:46:10,226
I get it. You can stop.

691
00:46:12,312 --> 00:46:14,814
I'll pretend I didn't hear it, so drop it.

692
00:46:18,902 --> 00:46:20,403
Did you see the guy's face?

693
00:46:21,112 --> 00:46:22,822
Without the mask, too?

694
00:46:23,573 --> 00:46:24,407
Yes.

695
00:46:24,532 --> 00:46:26,659
Tell me what he looked like.

696
00:46:27,952 --> 00:46:29,496
Describe any distinct features.

697
00:46:31,331 --> 00:46:32,749
Um…

698
00:46:34,667 --> 00:46:37,754
He had a slim face overall,

699
00:46:37,879 --> 00:46:40,715
with a slightly prominent chin.

700
00:46:40,840 --> 00:46:42,258
Oh, he had an underbite.

701
00:46:42,383 --> 00:46:43,468
Slow down.

702
00:46:44,636 --> 00:46:46,471
He had an underbite…

703
00:46:48,139 --> 00:46:49,766
with a prominent chin.

704
00:46:50,725 --> 00:46:51,809
What about his eyes?

705
00:46:51,935 --> 00:46:53,561
Nothing special about his eyes.

706
00:46:55,104 --> 00:46:57,232
His features were kind of close together…

707
00:46:57,357 --> 00:46:58,650
What else?

708
00:47:01,528 --> 00:47:03,029
Oh, a mole!

709
00:47:03,154 --> 00:47:04,906
He had a mole on his forehead.

710
00:47:25,885 --> 00:47:27,512
Hey, you're hurt.

711
00:47:28,596 --> 00:47:30,223
-Oh.
-Jeez.

712
00:47:40,066 --> 00:47:43,027
Hey, how on earth did you stop them?

713
00:47:43,778 --> 00:47:45,780
I was sure they'd appeal.

714
00:47:45,905 --> 00:47:48,491
He's not the type to let things go easily.

715
00:47:48,616 --> 00:47:50,743
That's a trade secret.

716
00:47:50,868 --> 00:47:52,203
You're something else.

717
00:47:52,912 --> 00:47:56,207
This is why I can't let you go.

718
00:47:57,750 --> 00:47:59,919
Okay, on that note,

719
00:48:00,545 --> 00:48:02,630
let me pour you a drink.

720
00:48:18,896 --> 00:48:20,023
Do you know her?

721
00:48:22,984 --> 00:48:25,778
I'm sorry. I'll escort her out.

722
00:48:25,903 --> 00:48:26,988
Oh.

723
00:48:31,492 --> 00:48:32,577
Get out right now.

724
00:48:35,246 --> 00:48:37,373
I went to beg Song Hae-na today.

725
00:48:38,458 --> 00:48:41,210
I wanted to plead with her
so I could direct again.

726
00:48:42,378 --> 00:48:45,006
As you said, I didn't want
to embarrass myself any further.

727
00:48:45,715 --> 00:48:47,884
I felt like it was my last chance.

728
00:48:48,009 --> 00:48:50,511
Okay, let's discuss this outside.

729
00:48:53,931 --> 00:48:55,642
But you ruined everything.

730
00:49:38,518 --> 00:49:39,602
What the hell?

731
00:49:40,436 --> 00:49:42,063
Bring that bitch back here!

732
00:49:42,647 --> 00:49:44,023
Right now. What the hell?

733
00:49:49,570 --> 00:49:50,405
Damn it.

734
00:50:00,957 --> 00:50:02,291
Are you crazy?

735
00:50:04,460 --> 00:50:06,087
Do you know what you just did?

736
00:50:06,212 --> 00:50:08,548
Yes, I know.

737
00:50:09,757 --> 00:50:11,467
You got screwed over.

738
00:50:11,592 --> 00:50:14,387
And I'm on my way
to screw you over even more.

739
00:50:15,555 --> 00:50:16,472
Why?

740
00:50:17,223 --> 00:50:19,767
Are you going to meet with Mr. Seo
and self-destruct?

741
00:50:20,935 --> 00:50:23,271
Since when did you care about Song Hae-na?

742
00:50:23,980 --> 00:50:26,941
It's funny coming from the person
who blackmailed her.

743
00:50:27,066 --> 00:50:28,693
I know I'm trash.

744
00:50:29,318 --> 00:50:32,196
Thanks to you, I snapped out of it.

745
00:50:32,321 --> 00:50:33,531
Thank you.

746
00:50:33,656 --> 00:50:36,242
Didn't you hear Song Hae-na earlier?

747
00:50:37,452 --> 00:50:39,078
She'll let you come back.

748
00:50:39,746 --> 00:50:42,457
She'll do whatever you want!

749
00:50:43,166 --> 00:50:44,709
So what's the problem?

750
00:50:49,255 --> 00:50:50,214
He'll hate it.

751
00:50:53,050 --> 00:50:54,844
If he finds out what I did,

752
00:50:55,928 --> 00:50:58,723
he'll hate it and be disappointed.

753
00:51:00,516 --> 00:51:01,601
I don't want that.

754
00:51:04,979 --> 00:51:06,230
It's your boyfriend.

755
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:13,988
Your weakness.

756
00:51:46,354 --> 00:51:47,897
It's not pathetic.

757
00:51:51,818 --> 00:51:52,985
Your dream.

758
00:51:56,531 --> 00:51:57,615
It's cool.

759
00:51:59,367 --> 00:52:00,952
It's really, really cool.

760
00:52:06,290 --> 00:52:08,084
Why didn't I realize sooner?

761
00:52:09,126 --> 00:52:11,462
You gave me so many clues.

762
00:52:13,339 --> 00:52:14,924
I was too slow to catch on.

763
00:52:16,843 --> 00:52:19,011
Since you call me trash anyway,

764
00:52:19,637 --> 00:52:21,013
I'll be straight with you.

765
00:52:24,517 --> 00:52:27,353
If you don't delete those photos
from the cloud today,

766
00:52:28,688 --> 00:52:32,233
starting tomorrow, your boyfriend
won't be able to show his face at work.

767
00:52:32,358 --> 00:52:34,485
And his future career?

768
00:52:34,610 --> 00:52:36,112
It'll be ruined.

769
00:52:36,237 --> 00:52:39,782
Why? Because I'll make sure of it.

770
00:52:39,907 --> 00:52:41,033
You…

771
00:52:44,203 --> 00:52:45,746
Wait.

772
00:52:45,872 --> 00:52:46,998
Are you crazy?

773
00:52:47,123 --> 00:52:48,207
What are you--

774
00:52:48,332 --> 00:52:50,126
Go right ahead if you want to die.

775
00:52:51,919 --> 00:52:53,254
If you mess with him,

776
00:52:53,838 --> 00:52:55,965
I will kill you.

777
00:52:56,757 --> 00:52:58,009
I'm not joking.

778
00:52:58,926 --> 00:53:00,720
I will seriously kill you.

779
00:53:07,935 --> 00:53:10,646
Now I'm really curious.

780
00:53:10,771 --> 00:53:13,107
Honestly, until a minute ago,

781
00:53:13,232 --> 00:53:15,610
I was just trying to scare you.

782
00:53:19,322 --> 00:53:20,907
But I changed my mind.

783
00:53:27,455 --> 00:53:28,998
Maybe I should mess with him.

784
00:53:30,791 --> 00:53:32,460
I think it would be fun.

785
00:53:32,585 --> 00:53:34,378
You bastard!

786
00:54:25,262 --> 00:54:26,389
Namgung.

787
00:54:32,853 --> 00:54:35,231
So don't feel too bad.

788
00:54:35,356 --> 00:54:36,983
It's not pathetic.

789
00:54:37,108 --> 00:54:40,027
Lots of people dream of that life.

790
00:54:45,032 --> 00:54:46,409
It's snowing.

791
00:54:55,668 --> 00:54:57,545
You know what?

792
00:54:58,587 --> 00:54:59,588
Haemado…

793
00:55:00,339 --> 00:55:03,300
is prettier in winter than in summer.

794
00:55:03,968 --> 00:55:05,886
Especially when it snows like this…

795
00:55:07,680 --> 00:55:09,140
it's even prettier.

796
00:55:20,443 --> 00:55:21,902
How pretty.

797
00:56:38,395 --> 00:56:39,730
You're awake.

798
00:56:45,694 --> 00:56:46,821
What?

799
00:56:47,446 --> 00:56:48,781
Why am I here?

800
00:56:49,532 --> 00:56:51,408
Answer the phone first.

801
00:56:53,786 --> 00:56:55,746
I think it's your boyfriend.

802
00:56:59,834 --> 00:57:00,876
DIRECTOR LEE MI-DO

803
00:57:05,965 --> 00:57:07,049
I guessed right.

804
00:57:09,802 --> 00:57:11,345
It is your boyfriend.

805
00:57:33,909 --> 00:57:37,413
QUEENS HAIR SALON

806
00:57:47,173 --> 00:57:50,009
It's the first snow.
Do you really not want to see me?

807
00:57:50,926 --> 00:57:52,094
I'm sorry.

808
00:57:53,804 --> 00:57:55,472
I know I was wrong.

809
00:58:06,817 --> 00:58:08,152
Mi-do.

810
00:58:15,659 --> 00:58:18,579
Why are you out here? It's cold.

811
00:58:19,997 --> 00:58:21,790
Your face is freezing.

812
00:58:22,625 --> 00:58:24,543
How could you go to work now?

813
00:58:28,547 --> 00:58:29,882
They'd fire me if I didn't.

814
00:58:33,344 --> 00:58:35,596
I barely got the ten days off.

815
00:58:36,347 --> 00:58:39,266
I want to beat you up so badly right now.

816
00:58:40,351 --> 00:58:42,478
I really want to punch you,

817
00:58:43,312 --> 00:58:45,606
but I'm so mad that I can't.

818
00:58:48,108 --> 00:58:49,235
I'm sorry.

819
00:58:55,532 --> 00:58:57,368
Hit me. I'll let you.

820
00:58:58,035 --> 00:58:59,286
Damn it, you…

821
00:59:05,417 --> 00:59:07,419
Did it hurt a lot?

822
00:59:10,422 --> 00:59:11,423
Yes.

823
00:59:13,342 --> 00:59:14,677
It hurt like hell.

824
00:59:18,138 --> 00:59:20,099
Does it hurt anywhere else?

825
00:59:21,809 --> 00:59:24,019
No, I'm fine.

826
00:59:24,770 --> 00:59:27,356
Even the doctor was shocked
by my recovery speed.

827
00:59:31,777 --> 00:59:33,654
Apparently,
if you only have one kidney left,

828
00:59:33,779 --> 00:59:37,324
it grows and takes over
up to 80% of the workload.

829
00:59:40,327 --> 00:59:41,578
I'm tall, you know.

830
00:59:43,747 --> 00:59:45,457
My kidney will grow a lot, too.

831
00:59:47,584 --> 00:59:48,836
Don't worry.

832
00:59:51,588 --> 00:59:53,173
Why did you do it?

833
01:00:00,639 --> 01:00:02,516
Because the peaches were so sweet.

834
01:00:06,228 --> 01:00:07,688
The peaches…

835
01:00:09,440 --> 01:00:11,191
were just so…

836
01:00:13,402 --> 01:00:14,486
sweet.

837
01:00:19,491 --> 01:00:22,328
I guess you still have
more to take from me.

838
01:00:22,453 --> 01:00:25,539
You ruined my credit
as soon as I became an adult.

839
01:00:27,166 --> 01:00:29,668
Was drowning me
in loan shark debt not enough?

840
01:00:30,627 --> 01:00:31,795
And you want what now?

841
01:00:35,966 --> 01:00:37,676
Just live like this until you die.

842
01:00:38,677 --> 01:00:40,054
I don't care at all.

843
01:01:02,201 --> 01:01:05,746
I went to Mr. Kim's and stole these.

844
01:01:06,538 --> 01:01:07,498
Good, right?

845
01:01:07,623 --> 01:01:09,041
Yes, it's good.

846
01:01:13,212 --> 01:01:14,380
Do you feel better?

847
01:01:14,963 --> 01:01:16,256
It's all better, right?

848
01:01:16,382 --> 01:01:18,967
Yes, I think I'm all better.

849
01:01:19,093 --> 01:01:21,970
You're the best, Mom.

850
01:01:28,060 --> 01:01:30,521
Those peaches I had…

851
01:01:32,648 --> 01:01:34,441
were just so damn sweet.

852
01:01:38,404 --> 01:01:40,906
If I knew they'd cost so much…

853
01:01:43,617 --> 01:01:45,077
I shouldn't have eaten them.

854
01:01:46,495 --> 01:01:47,329
Right?

855
01:02:14,731 --> 01:02:17,651
That was the first time
I saw Namgung Ho cry.

856
01:02:19,153 --> 01:02:21,321
From the day we met at seven years old

857
01:02:21,447 --> 01:02:23,031
until we turned 29,

858
01:02:23,157 --> 01:02:25,784
Namgung Ho never cried in front of me.

859
01:02:26,869 --> 01:02:29,746
But that night he cried in my arms
for the first time.

860
01:02:30,414 --> 01:02:32,499
He cried like a seven-year-old.

861
01:02:54,980 --> 01:02:57,232
THANK YOU TO CHOI HEE-JIN
FOR HER SPECIAL APPEARANCE

862
01:02:59,776 --> 01:03:00,819
Once you leave,

863
01:03:01,403 --> 01:03:03,071
will we never see each other again?

864
01:03:03,197 --> 01:03:04,907
I'm telling you, nothing happened.

865
01:03:05,032 --> 01:03:07,242
If you ever come across Park Su-a,

866
01:03:07,367 --> 01:03:08,869
don't you dare talk to her.

867
01:03:08,994 --> 01:03:10,078
Let's go.

868
01:03:10,662 --> 01:03:12,372
You're still looking beautiful, Mom.

869
01:03:12,498 --> 01:03:13,665
How have you been?

870
01:03:14,833 --> 01:03:17,169
It'd still be better
to pay it back together with Mi-do.

871
01:03:17,294 --> 01:03:20,923
How long have you been paying her?

872
01:03:21,048 --> 01:03:23,717
Do you think I came here
to catch Song Hae-na?

873
01:03:23,842 --> 01:03:25,427
You don't want to direct, do you?

874
01:03:26,512 --> 01:03:27,930
You're scared, aren't you?

875
01:03:29,848 --> 01:03:31,808
Subtitle translation by Cayle Kim
